        <body>
            <div xml:id="dr_d17">

                <pb facs="dr_d17-1" n="1" xml:id="dr_d17-1"/>

                <head>DR–17. Memorandum of a Conference with President Eisenhower<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="dr_d17-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1960-03"
                            >March 1960</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>OTHERS PRESENT</label>
                    <item>Secretary Herter</item>
                    <item>Mr. Allen Dulles</item>
                    <item>General Goodpaster</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President then discussed with Mr. Herter and Mr. Dulles questions raised by a
                    recent memorandum of him from Ed Clark.<anchor n="2" xml:id="dr_d17-f2"/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="dr_d17-f3"/> There have apparently been serious atrocities by the
                    Trujillo regime in recent days. The people around Trujillo are turning against
                    him. Trujillo’s family has taken large sums of money out of the country in
                    recent days. [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] that regime
                    may last as little as three weeks. [<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                        declassified</hi>] fearful that Castro or someone committed to Castro will
                    come into power soon thereafter. We have no moderate substitute for Trujillo
                    available. [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] considerable
                    merit <pb facs="0587" n="499" type="typeset" xml:id="pg499"/> in getting
                    Trujillo out of the country and trying to make a transition to some other
                    government.</p>
                <p>Mr. Herter also thought that on the whole course of events favored by Mr. Clark
                    seemed worth trying. He said we should not offer Trujillo asylum in the U.S.</p>
                <p>The President said that if Clark takes a part in this, he should not say that he
                    has any authority from the President, or has even seen the President lately.
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]</p>
                <pb facs="dr_d17-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="dr_d17-2"/>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>] The President said the
                    project might go ahead. It should be kept secret, and that Clark would be acting
                    on his own. [<hi rendition="#italic">text not declassified</hi>]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
