            <note corresp="#dr_d17-f3" n="3" xml:id="dr_d17-f3-content">
                <p>[illegible in the original], Ambassador to Peru, [illegible in the original], and
                    to Brazil [illegible in the original]. In a memorandum to Secretary Herter,
                    dated March [illegible in the original], 1960, Merchant [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >text not declassified</hi>] [illegible in the original]. According to the
                    memorandum, [illegible in the original] stated that he now gave Trujillo only
                    one to three weeks to [illegible in the original]. He added that he thought
                    Castro would be in the Dominican Republic a week after Trujillo’s fall.
                    ([illegible in the original])</p>
            </note>
